        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="191.386456692914" YPOS="814.49965984252" OwnPage="0" ItemID="1476170964" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="1043.48851307797" HEIGHT="400.50034015748" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="0" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L1043.49 0 L1043.49 400.5 L0 400.5 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L1043.49 0 L1043.49 400.5 L0 400.5 L0 0 Z" gXpos="191.386456692918" gYpos="814.49965984252" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Mosses are hotspots of nitrogen-fixation, due to diazotrophic symbionts in their microbiomes.  "/>
                <para PARENT="listBox"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Because of the large scale ecological service provided by these microbes, moss-cyanobacterial symbioses are of increasing interest. "/>
                <para PARENT="listBox"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Historically the most commonly studied such symbioses are "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="DejaVu Sans Mono Oblique" CH="Nostoc"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" spp. with &quot;feather&quot; (Hypnales) and "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="DejaVu Sans Mono Oblique" CH="Sphagnum"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" mosses. "/>
                <para PARENT="listBox"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Most studies have occurred in Scandinavia and the North American Boreal forest zone."/>
                <trail PARENT="listBox"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
